---
import Refugios from "../../../layouts/Refugios.astro";

/**
 * The platform is out of sign-in mail for now.
 *
 * ADR 0013: "When the ceiling is hit the honest behaviour is to tell the shelter to try
 * tomorrow, never to eat the digest." This page is that honesty, and it is a separate page
 * rather than a message on the sign-in form because the form is prerendered and has no way
 * to render a per-request state.
 *
 * **It reveals nothing about any address**, which is what allows it to exist at all
 * alongside ADR 0008's identical-response rule. Both refusals that lead here — the global
 * daily ceiling and the per-IP request limit — are facts about the platform and about the
 * caller, never about the submitted address, so a registered and an unregistered address
 * arrive here under exactly the same conditions. The per-address refusals, the five-minute
 * cooldown and the daily cap, deliberately do **not** land here: those are facts about one
 * address and are refused silently, with the same response a successful request gets.
 *
 * The wording says "in a few hours" rather than "tomorrow", because the budget is counted
 * over a trailing 24 hours rather than a calendar day — see `mailBudgetWindowStart()` for
 * why. Telling a shelter "tomorrow" when the answer is "in three hours" is a small lie that
 * costs it a day of publishing.
 */
---

<Refugios title="Vuelve más tarde" heading="Ahora mismo no podemos mandar el código">
  <p data-testid="mail-ceiling">
    Pawster manda una cantidad limitada de correos al día y hoy ya se llegó al tope. No es
    nada que hayas hecho tú y tu refugio está bien.
  </p>

  <p data-testid="try-later">
    Vuelve a intentarlo <strong>en unas horas</strong> y te va a llegar el código sin
    problema.
  </p>

  <p>
    <!--
      Named, not hidden behind "technical limits". The reservation is real and the reason is
      real: subscriber digests share the same 100 emails a day, and a shelter that
      understands the platform is small is not the same as a shelter that thinks it is
      broken.
    -->
    El tope existe porque el correo es lo único que este proyecto tiene contado, y una parte
    está reservada para los resúmenes que reciben los adoptantes.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/refugios/entrar">Volver</a></p>
</Refugios>
